## 4. Public User Page

### Current State Analysis
- **Leaderboard exists**: `GET /api/v1/leaderboard` shows top users with basic info
- **Badges API**: `GET /api/v1/users/me/badges` (private, requires auth)
- **No public profile**: No endpoint to view another user's profile
- **User privacy**: No `is_public` flag on user model

### Strategic Direction

#### Data Model Additions
Add to `User` model:
- `is_profile_public` (Boolean, default false)
- `public_slug` or use existing `id` for URL
- `bio` (optional short description)
- `social_links` (JSONB - optional)

#### Public Profile Content
- Display name and avatar
- Total XP and rank
- Earned badges (with earned dates)
- Earned certificates (with verification codes)
- Completion statistics (motifs discovered/learned/mastered)
- Optionally: Recent activity, favorite urn

#### API Endpoints Direction
- `GET /api/v1/users/{user_id}/public` - Get public profile (if enabled)
- `PATCH /api/v1/users/me/privacy` - Toggle profile visibility
- `GET /api/v1/certificates/{certificate_number}/verify` - Verify certificate authenticity

#### Frontend Direction
- New route: `/u/{userId}` or `/profile/{userId}`
- Public profile page component
- Share button with copy-to-clipboard
- Certificate verification page
- Privacy toggle in user settings

